> Conclusion

The shortcut adds a direct path, while post-add ReLU still gates signed signals. Projection
shortcuts change both sampling and channel count. Complete-depth checks and explicit subset
fits make those details visible; separate moving-state checkpoints are part of reproducible
inference. These small runs do not establish a depth advantage or ImageNet performance.

> References

